<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "https://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<node name="/com/lantharos/UsbProtection1">
  <!--
    USB protection: which new USB and Thunderbolt devices may connect.

    Mode: one of
      "off"           every device connects,
      "while-locked"  new devices wait while the screen is locked and at the login screen,
      "no-drives"     as while-locked, and drives, cameras and phones sharing files never connect,
      "known-only"    as while-locked, and only devices trusted on the port they are in connect.
    Devices wired inside the computer, on ports its firmware calls fixed, always count as trusted.
    SetMode changes it, asking for an administrator. Changing to "known-only" trusts every device
    connected at that moment.

    Held: devices waiting for an unlock, as (id, name), id being the sysfs device name such as
    "3-2", or "thunderbolt:0-1" for a Thunderbolt device.
    Waiting: devices nobody trusted in "known-only", as (id, name). While the computer is unlocked,
    the service asks the person at it for an administrator's approval of each, one at a time, and
    the device stays disconnected while it asks. Allow does the same for a device the caller names,
    and trusts it on the port it is in.
    Trusted: the trusted devices, as (key, name). Forget(key) stops trusting one; it stays connected
    until it is unplugged.

    SetLocked is for Kestrel: the shell of a desktop says when its screen locks and unlocks, and is
    the only caller accepted, told by the unit it runs in. A desktop counts as locked until its
    shell says otherwise, and again as soon as that shell leaves the bus, so a shell that crashes
    or is stopped leaves its desktop's devices waiting. The login screen always counts as locked,
    and a text console, which has no lock, never does.

    Released is emitted after unlocking, with the devices that were held back and are now available.
    The service also remembers them until TakeReleased returns them to the person signed in at the
    computer, so a session that starts after the unlock can still announce them. The list is cleared
    when devices start waiting again.
  -->
  <interface name="com.lantharos.UsbProtection1">
    <property name="Mode" type="s" access="read"/>
    <property name="Held" type="a(ss)" access="read"/>
    <property name="Waiting" type="a(ss)" access="read"/>
    <property name="Trusted" type="a(ss)" access="read"/>
    <method name="SetMode">
      <arg name="mode" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="Allow">
      <arg name="id" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="Forget">
      <arg name="key" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="SetLocked">
      <arg name="locked" type="b" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="TakeReleased">
      <arg name="devices" type="a(ss)" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <signal name="Released">
      <arg name="devices" type="a(ss)"/>
    </signal>
  </interface>
</node>
